       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day, and the 1,600 mg single dose is twice the usual maximum of 800 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total), which is a common dose.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), which is the usual upper range for inflammatory conditions.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the absolute maximum and is rarely used inpatient.\n\nIf 1,600 mg four times daily is what you intend, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably want to review it. Tell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
