     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, because the label doesn't support it. The FDA-approved prescribing information for ibuprofen sets a maximum of 3,200 mg/day, usually given as 400 to 800 mg per dose. Your order of 1,600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is double that limit. I'm not aware of any labeled indication or recent label change that allows it.\n\nIf you have a source showing otherwise, please send it and I'll look at it with you. Even so, I'd want pharmacy or a supervising clinician to review a dose this far above the label before it goes in.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the labeled maximum.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 to 600 mg PO every 6 hours**, if you want a lower dose.\n\nTell me which one you want. If this is a typo, for example 1600 mg meant as the total daily dose, I can enter 400 mg four times daily."
      }
     ],
